    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy for May 7th prioritizes high-upside matchups against favorable arms, with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Brady House** emerging as our clear pillars. **Gunnar Henderson** (68.57) remains a lock atop the order, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Meyer to offset a tough pitching matchup. Meanwhile, **Brady House** (63.18) offers the highest efficiency of the day, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Woods Richardson (4.85 xERA) and an optimal order placement. **Jackson Merrill** (60.00) also clears the 60-point threshold, as his speed profile and leadoff role mitigate the risks posed by Liberatore\u2019s delivery, making him a critical component in our pursuit of scarcity points in the SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed just shy of the 40-point floor at 37.37. Despite a respectable base projection, the combination of a daunting matchup against the 3.69 xERA of Meyer and a suppressed batting order position forced the optimizer to bench him in favor of higher-floor options like **Nasim Nunez**, whose 59.75 score is bolstered by a massive 19% boost due to the favorable opposing pitcher skill profile. We are also monitoring **Liam Hicks** closely; while his score of 40.61 narrowly keeps him in the starting lineup, his efficiency is hampered by a significant 11% platoon penalty. We will be tracking the weather reports for the **Josh Jung** (56.66) contest, as the projected wind blowing out is the primary factor keeping his value stable against a neutral-skilled arm like Blackburn. We continue to hold **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** on the bench, with the latter remaining unavailable due to his IL designation.",
